// Ch11 B10 side scene (optional): "The Lamp Bench" (E, 3 min, ~25 words). act2_ch11.md §4. Rhen and Liss
// repair a broken Lit Age lamp together in silence: the start of their truce. Three held inputs; the player
// is the steady hand. The lamp is EMPTY of bound light: Rhen fits his own lantern's spare oil burner, and
// Liss lights it. A wright's lamp with a diver's flame. No apology from either; Liss does NOT narrate the
// repair (her narrating is her grief tell, and belongs to Ch14-15). Silence is the scene.
title: ch11_lamp_bench
location: ch11/lowlight
---
@camera T05
@music silence fade=1.0
@anim liss pick_up lamp_housing
@mark rhen bench_end walk
@wait 2.0
<<event hold_input hold_steady>>
@anim liss seat_burner_seat
@wait 3.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
<<event hold_input turn_collar>>
@anim liss turn_collar
@wait 3.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
@anim rhen fit_oil_burner
<<event hold_input seat_it>>
@wait 3.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
@anim liss light lamp_housing
@sfx lamp_seat
@wait 3.0
Liss [neutral]: Pair-built. #line:ch11_bench_001 #tn:"A wright's term for things made as a matching pair: said of the two lamps, meant of the two of them."
Rhen [soft_smile]: Yeah. #line:ch11_bench_002
@wait 3.0
<<set $ch11_lamp_repaired = true>>
===
